# XCU diff
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# All tests run in the POSIX locale and TZ=UTC0 where times are shown. Inputs
# are small text files whose smallest list of changes is unique. The
# handling of a pure addition or deletion in -c output and of single-line
# ranges in -u output is not unambiguous on the page, so it is not tested.

assertion  XCU.diff.001
anchor     utilities/diff.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       Without options diff writes ed-like lines (NaM, NdM, NcM with ranges), then the affected lines of file1 as '< line' and of file2 as '> line', separated by --- for a change.
test       t/001-default-format.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.002
anchor     utilities/diff.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/diff.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       No output and status 0 for identical files, status 1 when differences are written, above 1 on an error.
test       t/002-exit-status.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.003
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-c
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-C
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       -c and -C n write file names with times, then hunks with context, once for each file, with ! marking changed lines.
test       t/003-context-format.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.004
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-u
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-U
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      2008
says       -u and -U n write file names with times, then @@ hunks with context and interleaved - and + lines, joining hunks whose context meets.
test       t/004-unified-format.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.005
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-e
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       -e writes an ed script from the end of the file to the start using a, c and d, text ended by a period line.
test       t/005-ed-script.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.006
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-f
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       -f writes the same kind of script from the start to the end with the command letter first and space-separated ranges.
test       t/006-forward-script.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.007
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-b
class      required
since      1992
says       -b ignores trailing white space and treats runs of white space as equal, but a blank is still different from none.
test       t/007-ignore-blanks.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.008
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPTIONS/-r
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       Directories are compared by file, reporting files present in one only; -r descends into common subdirectories; a file against a directory uses the same-named file.
test       t/008-directories.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.009
anchor     utilities/diff.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDIN
class      required
since      1992
says       A file operand - means the standard input.
test       t/009-stdin-operand.sh

assertion  XCU.diff.010
anchor     utilities/diff.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       For a differing common file in directory mode the line begins
           with "diff", the options as given on the command line and the
           two names; with -r, an unmatched file in a subdirectory is
           reported as "Only in" followed by the directory pathname
           relative to the operand and the file name.
test       t/010-dir-header-and-only-in.sh
